      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>This flag should be used on a secure decoder only. MediaCodec configured with this flag does decryption in a separate thread. The flag requires MediaCodec to operate asynchronously and will throw CryptoException if any, in the onCryptoError() callback. Applications should override the default implementation of onCryptoError() and access the associated CryptoException. CryptoException thrown will contain MediaCodec.CryptoInfo This can be accessed using getCryptoInfo()</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaCodec#CONFIGURE_FLAG_USE_CRYPTO_ASYNC" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.media.MediaCodec.CONFIGURE_FLAG_USE_CRYPTO_ASYNC</code>.</a></format></para>
